      "review_notes": "The independent target is total progeny of a Poisson Galton\u2013Watson tree, constructed from increasing finite-height tree measures. Finite-forest continuity uses diagonal cofinality; branching yields extinction mass q=exp(r(q-1)), and subcriticality forces q=1. This is not a queue-absorption recurrence definition. The CTE proof explores one root, uses the forest branching credit identity and Poisson offspring mean, and pays for termination with pending-population potential and amplification2-r. Independent tests check the first height-truncation mass exp(-r), zero-rate Dirac1, no zero progeny including infinite credit there, normalization, infinite expectation and generic framing. No explicit classical factorial-PMF identity is claimed."
    },
