      "review_notes": "The canonical uniform target reuses Lemire equal-fibre expectation. A fresh-product rejection wrapper and current-product wrapper isolate the retry logic. The initial low-word>=n case skips threshold evaluation safely because the Euclidean remainder is<n. Otherwise a deterministic helper proves the one-subtraction, two-subtraction and modulo-fallback thresholds all equal width%n. Independent clients instantiate n5/width8, n3/width8 and n3/width16, plus n=width and zero-bit singleton, and frame arbitrary resources with arbitrary ENNReal credits."
