      "review_notes": "The independent canonical Fisher PMF is proportional to choose(ones,k)*choose(zeros,n-k)*a^k*b^(n-k), zero outside0..n. A feasible k=min(n,ones) proves a positive normalizer. Deterministic program helpers execute four exact choose/power calls in their actual evaluation order and build the complete finite table; main CTE validates, builds and delegates to categorical sampling. Tests check arbitrary empty draws, both exhausted-color boundaries, complete population, and the odds2/1 example with ones2/zeros1/n1 giving marked probability4/5. Infinite credit at an impossible count and generic framed clients are checked."
